Fix round: close the six recorded product problems (toward v0.9.0)

1. SFTP key_file/known_hosts are WIRED (ADR-002 amendment part 3):
   restic's sftp.args option (present since 0.16.1, so apt's 0.16.4
   included) extends the native ssh argv — verified against restic's
   own source that the backend execs ssh via exec.Command and
   tokenizes the option string without any shell. The product builds
   `-o sftp.args="-o BatchMode=yes -i '<key>' -o
   UserKnownHostsFile='<hosts>'"` (single-quoted paths; validation
   rejects quote/newline characters, which the tokenizer cannot
   represent). The opts thread through every engine invocation
   (backup, init, snapshots, forget, prune, check, restore, the L4/L5
   scratch restores, the L6 rehearsal, doctor's probe). The declared
   files are stat-checked with a named error.

2. The SFTP end-to-end proof is AGENT-FREE: it declares key_file +
   known_hosts through the product and owns a temporary known_hosts
   file (the user's real ~/.ssh/known_hosts is never mutated). The
   proof now runs locally on Windows (the disabled OpenSSH agent
   service is irrelevant) and hosted; the raw-restic verification
   step passes the same -o sftp.args.

3. The sidecar capture honors a user-declared image (volume `image`
   field, sidecar-only like the container rule; defaults to alpine).
   The docker argv is factored into a pure, unit-tested function.

4. Lock start-time verification (ADR-007 revisit condition): the lock
   records the holder's process start time (Linux /proc/<pid>/stat;
   Windows PowerShell StartTime; other unix degrades to liveness,
   honestly). On contention a live pid whose start time differs from
   the record is a REUSED pid — reclaimed. Pid-only locks from
   earlier builds fall back to liveness alone.

5. The named-volume direct-capture proof executes on the hosted
   runner: CI grants docker-data traversal (sudo chmod o+rx
   /var/lib/docker /var/lib/docker/volumes, non-fatal); the proof's
   reachability gate still skips honestly where traversal cannot
   work.

6. Stale text cleanup: the module headers and comments promising
   "later phases" that have arrived, cli.md's dead
   declared-but-not-captured paragraph, the hosting-era workflow
   comments.

Tests: 183 passing (11 new: 2 config validation, 4 lock core, 5
CLI sftp/sidecar builders, 1 pid-reuse integration) — all gates
green locally (fmt/clippy -D warnings/test/vet/deny/workflow
validator/bench check).
